# Round 81: vec_loop discarded the counter increment's POSITION --
# the emitters hard-code increment-LAST, so a write after
# `i is i + 1` reads the POST-increment counter in the VM (VM
# 0 1 2 3, AOT 0 1 2 0, both rc 0; straddling writes hit wrong
# lanes in both directions), and two increments would make a step-2
# loop the hoist ran as step-1. Admission requires exactly one
# increment in final position; every other interleaving demotes to
# the scalar path, byte-exact by construction. The axis no fixture
# had varied in 28 rounds (invariants 16/19).
b is buffer of 4
i is 0
loop while i < 3:
    i is i + 1
    b[i] is i
print of b[0]
print of b[1]
print of b[2]
print of b[3]
print of i

b is buffer of 8
c is buffer of 8
i is 0
loop while i < 6:
    b[i] is i * 2
    i is i + 1
    c[i] is i + 10
print of b[0]
print of b[5]
print of c[0]
print of c[1]
print of c[6]
print of i
